   "question": "Is there a real-world financial code component, short but mathematically deep, on which Muse Code alone is very unlikely to produce a verified repair within $10 and 4 hours, while Muse Code with everything ProofForge offers has a substantially higher chance?",
   "questionMore": [
    "The measured evidence so far does not show such a gap. Muse Code alone verified Knight (2 of 2), Cetus (1 of 1) and Balancer (1 of 3); Muse Code with ProofForge verified Knight 2 of 2, Cetus 1 of 1, Balancer 2 of 3 (`results/muse-code-1`). Compound is not verified by any arm: the sequence-level reward bounds stay open in every run (`results/library-1`, `web/generated/shapes/summary.json`). On the frozen benchmark the arms do not separate (`results/e1-test-1`)."
   ],
   "runs": 20,
   "runsText": "Number: 5 runs per arm per task, so 20 runs if both tasks are built (10 if only `rw-oz-sqrt` is). The number is fixed; there is no extension and no early stopping on results.",
